Granular:
1) A borrow is associated with the user identified by the JWT.
2) A user can only create a borrow for themselves.
3) A user can only view their own borrows.
4) A user can only return/delete their own borrows.
5) The user ID used for ownership comes from the authenticated JWT, not the request body.
6) Books themselves are shared library resources and are not owned by individual users.
